title The name that left, and the four facts that stayed
prompt Keaton -- kg, we can molt breach veganreyklah2 and reyklah and mitra shed prep
think A rename is a promise to every inbound reference, so the sweep went whole-tree first -- the one standing exception to read scope. 602 occurrences across 243 tracked files, 187 of them dated testimony that keeps every word.
think The successor needed no invention: a living line already read name veganreyklah2 -> grain, so the breach was finishing a move the tree had started rather than choosing a name.
think Took the worst carrier first, and it was the ratchet I was already turning. Six files declared the SAME constant /tmp/veganreyklah2-ns-poll-stop -- five Caravan poll witnesses and one Mantra stop witness.
think Checked for a coordination contract before touching it, since a stop file shared between two scripts on purpose would break under a per-run name. Each proved self-contained: it builds, removes the sentinel at prep, runs, writes the sentinel to halt its own service.
think So the shared spelling bought collision and nothing else. Two running at once, or one on each of eight ships, has one run's prep rm delete the stop signal another just wrote -- a service that never stops hangs its witness, and one stopped early inverts its result.
think Ran one witness BEFORE changing it, to learn whether this pier could prove the repair at all. It could, which is what let the lap proceed -- the glow_host lesson from an hour ago, applied ahead of the work rather than after it.
obs THE FINDING IS THE SPLIT, not the rename. Four kinds of occurrence must keep the elder word or the tree starts lying: PUBKEYS.md carries Kaeden Reyklah and a real handle inside the record whose whole job is to name them; domain-registry.bron carries reyklah.com and .net, which are real registrations; every comment saying what a thing molted FROM needs the elder word to say anything; and 187 dated files plus git history are where a superseded name belongs.
obs A blind sed over 602 occurrences would have falsified an identity record, a domain registry, and three teaching comments in one pass. That is why the census came before the change and why roughly thirty yonder files stay unbreached, awaiting a word.
obs Reyklah alone is a person's surname. The word arrived in the grant beside the repository name, and those are two different things; only the second is ours to move.
obs Largest single fall this ratchet has taken: files 47 to 41, wipers 13 to 7. Across the round the pair came down from 49 and 15.
